    "zoom": 15,
    "method": "The per-channel shift from the summer sheet to the Winter national map, measured as the channel-wise median of fill pixels over the same tiles in both, then applied to the palette's summer value. The shift is what is comparable: these tiles are JPEG while the summer palette was measured from the lossless swissTLM3D raster. Pale variants keep the relationship they have to their measured parent. Overlay colours, ink, the road hierarchy and contours are printed as in summer and are unchanged.",
